bio of different participants.

00:21:23.410 --> 00:21:30.770
You can scroll to see who
different participants are,

00:21:30.770 --> 00:21:35.770
where they're coming from, what
their story is, how they felt

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:40.070
and relate to this project.

00:21:40.070 --> 00:21:45.130
And you can then
see their experience

00:21:45.130 --> 00:21:47.500
by clicking on this button.

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:50.350
If you scroll down
more, you can then

00:21:50.350 --> 00:21:57.280
find a video of me telling you
about how this project started

00:21:57.280 --> 00:22:03.850
and series of the
group photo shoots

00:22:03.850 --> 00:22:07.510
and the lists of the names
of all the peoples who

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:09.820
contributed to this project.

00:22:09.820 --> 00:22:11.860
And then there's
a Navigator that

00:22:11.860 --> 00:22:15.100
can help you navigate
to different walls

00:22:15.100 --> 00:22:16.930
of the exhibition.

00:22:16.930 --> 00:22:23.440
Now let's go and see
Alexa's experience.

00:22:23.440 --> 00:22:26.470
When you enter the
participants wall,

00:22:26.470 --> 00:22:33.790
you can see all of their photos
by clicking right and left

00:22:33.790 --> 00:22:35.920
into this slider.

00:22:35.920 --> 00:22:41.110
You can then scroll down
and see their walls,

00:22:41.110 --> 00:22:45.100
where you can find their
bio and all of their photos

00:22:45.100 --> 00:22:47.650
next to each other.

00:22:47.650 --> 00:22:53.110
Some photos have reflections,
which are in the form of poetry

00:22:53.110 --> 00:22:57.490
or a short essay, mixed photos.

00:22:57.490 --> 00:23:02.710
These reflections are
written by other artist.

00:23:02.710 --> 00:23:07.990
You can also click on the
