The behind the scene helped.

00:26:20.550 --> 00:26:26.700
Now I want to jump start
the Q&amp;A by asking you

00:26:26.700 --> 00:26:29.370
a question from one of the
amazing participants who

00:26:29.370 --> 00:26:31.680
could make it here today.

00:26:31.680 --> 00:26:35.250
Dodo, I'm so glad you
could make it here today.

00:26:35.250 --> 00:26:37.020
I have a question for you.

00:26:40.140 --> 00:26:42.120
I was wondering
if you could share

00:26:42.120 --> 00:26:47.720
your experience with Trapped and
how your photos made you feel.

00:26:47.720 --> 00:26:49.790
Yeah, of course.

00:26:49.790 --> 00:26:51.800
I was watching, in
the video, where

00:26:51.800 --> 00:26:55.590
some of the other
participants shared as well.

00:26:55.590 --> 00:27:01.600
So, I'll try to live up
to that level of insight.

00:27:01.600 --> 00:27:03.510
So, yeah, thank you
for inviting me.

00:27:03.510 --> 00:27:08.960
This has really been
a journey for you

00:27:08.960 --> 00:27:10.040
and all the participants.

00:27:10.040 --> 00:27:12.770
I know for myself,
actually, it's

00:27:12.770 --> 00:27:18.230
a journey that started very
early when I was much younger.

00:27:18.230 --> 00:27:23.960
And Trapped very promptly at
the time, a couple of years ago,

00:27:23.960 --> 00:27:28.160
helped me put words to
it, to put an image to it.

00:27:28.160 --> 00:27:31.760
And then something that
continues after Trapped, I

00:27:31.760 --> 00:27:35.530
think for my own reflection
to grow after that.

00:27:35.530 --> 00:27:39.530
So I'm very happy to
see you again and also

00:27:39.530 --> 00:27:42.660
share that with everyone here.

00:27:42.660 --> 00:27:45.230
So first off, I guess
the experience itself

00:27:45.230 --> 00:27:50.390
I would say it was very
fun and reflective.

00:27:50.390 --> 00:27:53.000
Fun being that from
the video, I think

00:27:53.000 --> 00:27:57.080
everybody saw that it was a
very collaborative process.

00:27:57.080 --> 00:28:01.040
I didn't feel like I was
the model doing whatever

00:28:01.040 --> 00:28:02.210
Elaheh wanted me to do.

00:28:02.210 --> 00:28:06.730
That was not the
point of the project.

00:28:06.730 --> 00:28:09.170
So I think you, Elaheh,
very intentionally

00:28:09.170 --> 00:28:11.270
wanted it to be a
thought partnership

00:28:11.270 --> 00:28:16.790
and play around with it, like
it's a true collaboration.

00:28:16.790 --> 00:28:20.540
So I love that we were
just experimenting,

00:28:20.540 --> 00:28:23.230
the idea of having makeup.

00:28:23.230 --> 00:28:28.460
It was when we were talking at
some point, I don't even know,

00:28:28.460 --> 00:28:32.120
I don't even remember
who popped up the idea,

00:28:32.120 --> 00:28:35.370
but you know we went with it
and it turned out really well.

00:28:35.370 --> 00:28:39.650
So yeah, the whole experience
itself I think has a lot of fun

00:28:39.650 --> 00:28:40.790
to it.

00:28:40.790 --> 00:28:45.650
But of course at the same time I
think because of your outreach,

00:28:45.650 --> 00:28:51.440
it's helped me really start
to reflect on this feeling

00:28:51.440 --> 00:28:54.980
that I've had for
a really long time.

00:28:54.980 --> 00:28:58.910
And personally, I
was also the girl

00:28:58.910 --> 00:29:02.995
in tech, or math,
very, very early on.

00:29:02.995 --> 00:29:05.570
I went through this whole
competitive math track,

00:29:05.570 --> 00:29:10.430
came from China to US for
high school, and then MIT.

00:29:10.430 --> 00:29:14.690
And on top of all that,
I also reflected myself

00:29:14.690 --> 00:29:19.220
to be an artist at heart
who's studying engineering

00:29:19.220 --> 00:29:26.600
at MIT, who has an interest
in business, who growing up

00:29:26.600 --> 00:29:31.640
in a society where I had a
lot of expectations of women

00:29:31.640 --> 00:29:35.930
not necessarily in
tech, or math, or art.

00:29:38.570 --> 00:29:43.220
So I felt like
through the project

00:29:43.220 --> 00:29:48.800
I was able to really see it
through the power of arts

00:29:48.800 --> 00:29:52.940
in one, two, three
images and a couple

00:29:52.940 --> 00:29:59.550
short blurbs what this
conflict has been about.

00:29:59.550 --> 00:30:02.340
And I think the
point that it was

00:30:02.340 --> 00:30:05.630
the struggle between
the outside expectations

00:30:05.630 --> 00:30:09.530
and my own way of
looking at myself.

00:30:09.530 --> 00:30:16.160
The multiple identities that
could exist in the same person,

00:30:16.160 --> 00:30:21.110
but we live in a world
of specialization.

00:30:21.110 --> 00:30:26.600
We live in the world of putting
a single label on people.

00:30:26.600 --> 00:30:32.480
But in fact, I felt like I'm
much more than a single label.

00:30:32.480 --> 00:30:36.170
I'm much more than a
specialized career.

00:30:36.170 --> 00:30:40.380
I'm much more than
any part of me.

00:30:40.380 --> 00:30:43.220
So thank you for jump
starting that reflection.

00:30:43.220 --> 00:30:45.920
I would say that
reflection actually

00:30:45.920 --> 00:30:51.590
since college has really in the
past two or three years since I

00:30:51.590 --> 00:30:55.070
started working, so I
worked for about three years

00:30:55.070 --> 00:30:58.880
at a global consulting
firm, I just

00:30:58.880 --> 00:31:04.910
recently decided to change my
career into k-12 education,

00:31:04.910 --> 00:31:07.010
also professional coaching.

00:31:07.010 --> 00:31:09.830
And I think actually
this whole reflection

00:31:09.830 --> 00:31:13.790
of who I really
am, who I can be,

00:31:13.790 --> 00:31:19.430
all the different parts of
me, really led me here, right.

00:31:19.430 --> 00:31:25.430
I think just even in my
previous career as a consultant,

00:31:25.430 --> 00:31:32.120
I was continuing to reflect on
how those outside expectations

00:31:32.120 --> 00:31:35.690
of what you should behave,
what you should like.

00:31:38.450 --> 00:31:43.020
Your job title becomes
your only identity.

00:31:43.020 --> 00:31:46.490
And I was actually
very happy that I

00:31:46.490 --> 00:31:51.320
could be bring this discussion
to my colleagues, to my team,

00:31:51.320 --> 00:31:52.490
to the company itself.

00:31:52.490 --> 00:31:57.020
We actually had a discussion
around multiple identity.

00:31:57.020 --> 00:32:02.900
How people see themselves
versus what they think the job

00:32:02.900 --> 00:32:06.800
requires them to be perceived.

00:32:06.800 --> 00:32:10.160
And these discussions
continue and I

00:32:10.160 --> 00:32:15.770
think if I were to sum up of
how I look at this picture of me

00:32:15.770 --> 00:32:21.740
and of your home
wall picture as well,

00:32:21.740 --> 00:32:26.330
I would say that it reminds
me of a quote I saw somewhere,

00:32:26.330 --> 00:32:29.870
which is, the darkness
that we experience

00:32:29.870 --> 00:32:33.050
is not the darkness
of the tomb but rather

00:32:33.050 --> 00:32:35.480
the darkness of the womb.

00:32:35.480 --> 00:32:37.100
We are to be born.

00:32:37.100 --> 00:32:39.620
We are to be awakened.

00:32:39.620 --> 00:32:42.800
The fact that we are
doing this project,

00:32:42.800 --> 00:32:47.600
experiencing these struggles,
and conflicts, and emotions

00:32:47.600 --> 00:32:51.140
is the start of something
new and the start

00:32:51.140 --> 00:32:55.380
of the liberation of all of us.

00:32:55.380 --> 00:32:58.970
And so now I look
at these pictures

00:32:58.970 --> 00:33:02.390
I feel extremely hopeful.

00:33:02.390 --> 00:33:08.450
So for me it has been
the past three years

00:33:08.450 --> 00:33:13.280
and the journey didn't
start with the project.

00:33:13.280 --> 00:33:16.460
It was very well captured
with the project.

00:33:16.460 --> 00:33:20.780
And it continued
after the project.

00:33:20.780 --> 00:33:24.125
Thank you so much
Dodo for sharing that.

00:33:24.125 --> 00:33:25.430
Of course.

00:33:25.430 --> 00:33:27.623
It was amazing to hear.

00:33:27.623 --> 00:33:28.415
Thank you inviting.

00:33:28.415 --> 00:33:29.830
Yeah.

00:33:29.830 --> 00:33:33.260
I'm so glad you could make it.

