00:34:16.500 --> 00:34:17.750
I joined the exhibition today.

00:34:17.750 --> 00:34:21.199
And there's a question
growing in my mind

00:34:21.199 --> 00:34:26.840
and that's why the dark
theme or the black color

00:34:26.840 --> 00:34:30.530
is chosen to represent
the participants

00:34:30.530 --> 00:34:34.270
in this exhibition.

00:34:34.270 --> 00:34:36.580
What does exactly
this color means

00:34:36.580 --> 00:34:40.159
and what emotion this color
is going to express there?

00:34:40.159 --> 00:34:42.850
So I told everybody
to wear whatever

00:34:42.850 --> 00:34:44.270
they're comfortable with.

00:34:44.270 --> 00:34:46.150
So whatever, it's them.

00:34:46.150 --> 00:34:51.489
For example, if I'm a person
that I usually wear dresses

00:34:51.489 --> 00:34:53.590
and that's what
I'm comfortable in,

00:34:53.590 --> 00:34:55.420
then I wanted the person
to wear the dress.

00:34:55.420 --> 00:34:58.300
Or if they're usually
comfortable walking around

00:34:58.300 --> 00:35:01.300
with jerseys then that's what
I wanted them to show up with.

00:35:01.300 --> 00:35:04.120
And I think in the
final photo shoot

00:35:04.120 --> 00:35:09.430
you can see that contrast
of what different women are

00:35:09.430 --> 00:35:15.370
comfortable wearing and
feel like that's them.

00:35:15.370 --> 00:35:16.360
That's what they are.

00:35:19.137 --> 00:35:19.970
Thank you very much.

00:35:19.970 --> 00:35:21.370
That was a great exhibition.

00:35:21.370 --> 00:35:24.650
Yeah, of course,
thank you for joining.

00:35:24.650 --> 00:35:26.920
I have a question
about your contribution

00:35:26.920 --> 00:35:29.410
to the arts in your life at MIT.

00:35:29.410 --> 00:35:35.470
Were you surprised by what
prominence this practice took

00:35:35.470 --> 00:35:37.600
in your life as a student?

00:35:37.600 --> 00:35:40.330
Was that something you expected
or was that a discovery

00:35:40.330 --> 00:35:41.290
for you?

00:35:41.290 --> 00:35:43.600
It was not something
that I expected.

00:35:43.600 --> 00:35:46.120
It when I found--

00:35:46.120 --> 00:35:48.970
so growing up, I knew
I loved photography.

00:35:48.970 --> 00:35:51.220
I would always take
a photo on my phone

00:35:51.220 --> 00:35:56.260
or steal my mom's camera
and take photos with that.

00:35:56.260 --> 00:35:57.710
So I knew I liked it.

00:35:57.710 --> 00:36:04.690
But I realized how powerful it
can be in my photography class.

00:36:04.690 --> 00:36:07.600
Again, thanks to my
amazing professors

00:36:07.600 --> 00:36:10.630
who opened my eyes
to the power of arts.

00:36:10.630 --> 00:36:15.400
And that was then that I
realized the issues that I care

00:36:15.400 --> 00:36:21.250
about, I probably can
contribute doing robotics

00:36:21.250 --> 00:36:25.030
and the engineering that
I'm studying and I'm doing,

00:36:25.030 --> 00:36:28.920
but I realize there
is like something

00:36:28.920 --> 00:36:31.860
more powerful with
just like a photo.

00:36:31.860 --> 00:36:34.080
That you can show it
to different people ,

00:36:34.080 --> 00:36:36.780
everybody would take
something different from it,

00:36:36.780 --> 00:36:39.630
and it's just so powerful
because there's like no right

00:36:39.630 --> 00:36:41.460
or wrong, no this or that.

00:36:41.460 --> 00:36:44.370
This is what I'm showing you.

00:36:44.370 --> 00:36:49.810
I put a lot of emotions in it,
now what do you take out of it.

00:36:49.810 --> 00:36:53.640
And I think that was
something that in photography

00:36:53.640 --> 00:36:57.430
and the visual arts that
I started practicing,

00:36:57.430 --> 00:37:01.585
I saw a lot more than I ever
saw in my engineering classes

00:37:01.585 --> 00:37:02.085
or research.

00:37:05.100 --> 00:37:06.662
That's a good answer, thanks.

00:37:06.662 --> 00:37:07.620
Thank you, [INAUDIBLE].

00:37:07.620 --> 00:37:09.810
Really interesting.

00:37:09.810 --> 00:37:11.370
And since I'm here
to moderate, I

00:37:11.370 --> 00:37:13.690
want to welcome anyone
else to ask a question.

00:37:13.690 --> 00:37:16.680
You can also ask of
anyone who participated

00:37:16.680 --> 00:37:17.980
who wants to speak up.

00:37:17.980 --> 00:37:20.800
We'd love to hear from you.

00:37:20.800 --> 00:37:27.210
Thank you Elaheh for your
invitation to the opening.

00:37:27.210 --> 00:37:32.100
It's very brave of you to
express yourself so publicly.

00:37:32.100 --> 00:37:35.640
My question for you is that, you
said that when you started it,

00:37:35.640 --> 00:37:37.410
it was a personal project.

00:37:37.410 --> 00:37:40.380
And then you realized that
other people were also

00:37:40.380 --> 00:37:42.600
struggling with
issues and you started

00:37:42.600 --> 00:37:47.010
to invite them to also
join this and feel

00:37:47.010 --> 00:37:49.470
this experience with you.

00:37:49.470 --> 00:37:52.410
So my question is
that, what made you

00:37:52.410 --> 00:37:54.180
feel that the project was done?

00:37:54.180 --> 00:37:56.260
Because it can go on forever.

00:37:56.260 --> 00:37:59.410
And what made you
stop and decide that,

00:37:59.410 --> 00:38:01.590
OK, it's time to wrap it up.

00:38:01.590 --> 00:38:03.340
That's a good question.

00:38:03.340 --> 00:38:08.040
I think it was a very
hard call to make.

00:38:08.040 --> 00:38:14.010
I think one thing that
I realized in 2020,

00:38:14.010 --> 00:38:16.590
before I actually make the
call of having the final photo

00:38:16.590 --> 00:38:24.050
shoot, was that my goal was
to have a space for everybody

00:38:24.050 --> 00:38:25.220
to feel safe.

00:38:25.220 --> 00:38:29.120
And I felt like my
project maybe is also

00:38:29.120 --> 00:38:35.000
creating some sort of
gender exclusiveness,

00:38:35.000 --> 00:38:36.800
that I'm just
making it for women

00:38:36.800 --> 00:38:39.860
to feel, to show the
struggles of women

00:38:39.860 --> 00:38:42.710
and show the struggles
of female in the society.

00:38:42.710 --> 00:38:48.440
And I realized I want
it to be more than that.

00:38:48.440 --> 00:38:54.830
Even though yes, women have had
a lot of struggles in history,

00:38:54.830 --> 00:39:00.740
we can just go and see how much
bias has affected all of us.

00:39:00.740 --> 00:39:04.190
But the society that
we're living now,

00:39:04.190 --> 00:39:07.400
we know that the gender
is not binary anymore.

00:39:07.400 --> 00:39:11.510
We have non-binary
identification

00:39:11.510 --> 00:39:14.490
and those people are also
having struggles of their own.

00:39:14.490 --> 00:39:18.350
And it's just a wide range
of people and just people

00:39:18.350 --> 00:39:20.490
having struggles.

00:39:20.490 --> 00:39:23.390
And I wanted my
next project to be

00:39:23.390 --> 00:39:26.930
more about that creating a
safer space for everybody.

00:39:26.930 --> 00:39:29.750
Creating something
that everybody

00:39:29.750 --> 00:39:34.130
can contribute to, and
have other audiences to see

00:39:34.130 --> 00:39:39.320
that and be like, OK, we need
to be more cautious or conscious

00:39:39.320 --> 00:39:41.810
of all of these issues and
we need to speak up about all

00:39:41.810 --> 00:39:42.500
of these issues.

00:39:45.290 --> 00:39:49.690
OK, thank you and do you
have anything in your mind

00:39:49.690 --> 00:39:54.090
that you'd be proceeding
with your next project?

00:39:54.090 --> 00:39:55.572
A future project.

00:39:55.572 --> 00:39:56.530
That's a good question.

00:39:56.530 --> 00:39:57.816
[LAUGHTER]

00:39:57.816 --> 00:39:58.802
OK, sorry.

00:39:58.802 --> 00:40:02.750
[LAUGHTER]

00:40:02.750 --> 00:40:03.760
That's a good question.

00:40:03.760 --> 00:40:06.820
That's my answer.

00:40:06.820 --> 00:40:09.550
Fair enough.

00:40:09.550 --> 00:40:11.080
I actually have
the same question

00:40:11.080 --> 00:40:13.705
I was going to ask her, what are
you going to do with your time

00:40:13.705 --> 00:40:18.130
now that a project has its
showcase and it's over?

00:40:18.130 --> 00:40:21.070
Yeah, I know it's--

00:40:21.070 --> 00:40:21.955
I'm going to sleep.

00:40:21.955 --> 00:40:25.565
[LAUGHTER]

00:40:28.420 --> 00:40:30.130
Yeah, I'm going to
do a lot of that

00:40:30.130 --> 00:40:34.930
and once I have a lot of sleep,
I'll think about something else

00:40:34.930 --> 00:40:37.820
to do.

00:40:37.820 --> 00:40:39.740
Do you think that
this project will

00:40:39.740 --> 00:40:42.590
extend into your
professional life in any way?

00:40:42.590 --> 00:40:44.970
Any of the lessons
that you've learned

00:40:44.970 --> 00:40:47.173
go into your professional work?

00:40:47.173 --> 00:40:49.340
I mean, obviously you're
finishing your degree still

00:40:49.340 --> 00:40:49.840
and--

00:40:49.840 --> 00:40:51.710
Yeah, I think so.

00:40:51.710 --> 00:40:55.790
I think this project gave me
a lot of courage to just talk

00:40:55.790 --> 00:40:58.700
to people as people.

00:40:58.700 --> 00:41:03.500
Because I think
sometimes it's just hard

00:41:03.500 --> 00:41:08.750
to see other people as
somebody else who's also

00:41:08.750 --> 00:41:10.550
struggling and dealing
with everything

00:41:10.550 --> 00:41:12.380
that you are also dealing with.

00:41:12.380 --> 00:41:18.687
And I think doing this project
I would just go to people

00:41:18.687 --> 00:41:20.270
and start talking
to them and be like,

00:41:20.270 --> 00:41:22.880
Yeah, there is this
project that I'm working on

00:41:22.880 --> 00:41:25.020
and it would just open
up the conversation

00:41:25.020 --> 00:41:28.800
and help me get to know
people, connect to more people.

00:41:28.800 --> 00:41:33.710
And I think that was a
practice for me to just learn

00:41:33.710 --> 00:41:38.450
how to talk to people
because as somebody who

00:41:38.450 --> 00:41:42.890
moved from Iran to US and
as somebody who's English

00:41:42.890 --> 00:41:46.730
is my second language, it was
a challenge for me to just talk

00:41:46.730 --> 00:41:49.220
to people when I
first moved to US.

00:41:49.220 --> 00:41:56.390
And make friends and network, or
just in a party talk to people.

00:41:56.390 --> 00:42:00.110
And I think this project
gave me a really good medium

00:42:00.110 --> 00:42:03.605
in practice and I'm grateful.

00:42:06.310 --> 00:42:08.690
Dodo has a question.

00:42:08.690 --> 00:42:13.060
Yeah, so I guess
on a related topic,

00:42:13.060 --> 00:42:17.440
how do you see arts, maybe
photography obviously

00:42:17.440 --> 00:42:21.130
is a big part of it or
maybe other art forms,

00:42:21.130 --> 00:42:25.230
play into your
life or profession?

00:42:25.230 --> 00:42:28.750
Whether a professional
life or from this point on,

00:42:28.750 --> 00:42:34.000
what is the role of
continuing to be an artist?

00:42:34.000 --> 00:42:35.620
What does that mean to you?

00:42:35.620 --> 00:42:37.130
What's your plan around that?

00:42:37.130 --> 00:42:40.840
That's a really great question.

00:42:40.840 --> 00:42:43.330
These are actually things that
I'm actively thinking about.

00:42:43.330 --> 00:42:44.570
What am I going to do next?

00:42:44.570 --> 00:42:47.770
How is this going to merge
with my engineering life?

00:42:47.770 --> 00:42:51.980
And the honest answer is
that I still don't know.

00:42:51.980 --> 00:42:53.660
I'm still trying
to figure it out.

00:42:53.660 --> 00:42:58.340
But some ideas
that I have now is

00:42:58.340 --> 00:43:02.930
that I really enjoy talking
to different people.

00:43:02.930 --> 00:43:06.230
Bringing different people from
different backgrounds together

00:43:06.230 --> 00:43:10.640
and having them connect
and have something amazing

00:43:10.640 --> 00:43:12.340
come out of it.

00:43:12.340 --> 00:43:17.720
And I think I want to use
that to bring people together.

00:43:17.720 --> 00:43:20.750
Whether it's going to be
an engineering project,

00:43:20.750 --> 00:43:24.630
an art project, or something
completely different.

00:43:24.630 --> 00:43:26.420
But I want to bring
people together.

00:43:26.420 --> 00:43:30.230
Because when I talk to
people individually,

00:43:30.230 --> 00:43:33.440
I can see how amazing
they are and sometimes I

00:43:33.440 --> 00:43:35.630
can see how they're
not confident

00:43:35.630 --> 00:43:38.000
and they don't see
how amazing they are.

00:43:38.000 --> 00:43:41.390
And I want to be
like, if I can, I

00:43:41.390 --> 00:43:44.360
want to be able to tell
them that you're amazing.

00:43:44.360 --> 00:43:46.220
And then tell
somebody else who I

00:43:46.220 --> 00:43:49.040
know it's amazing be
like, you two are awesome,

00:43:49.040 --> 00:43:51.600
meet each other, make
something amazing.

00:43:51.600 --> 00:43:54.530
And I think I could do a
little bit of that in Trapped

00:43:54.530 --> 00:43:57.692
and I want to do more of that.

00:43:57.692 --> 00:44:00.240
All right, cool, yeah.

00:44:00.240 --> 00:44:01.752
I can relate.

00:44:01.752 --> 00:44:07.130
I think that's the power of arts
in that case is very strong.

00:44:07.130 --> 00:44:08.070
Thank you.

00:44:08.070 --> 00:44:10.740
Yeah, thank you for asking me.

00:44:10.740 --> 00:44:12.637
I'd say the world needs you.

00:44:12.637 --> 00:44:14.100
No.

00:44:14.100 --> 00:44:15.150
Needs more of that.

00:44:18.820 --> 00:44:21.354
Anyone else?

00:44:21.354 --> 00:44:22.140
Hi, Elaheh.

00:44:22.140 --> 00:44:23.670
This is really great.

00:44:23.670 --> 00:44:27.300
Thank you for sharing
these pictures with us,

00:44:27.300 --> 00:44:29.560
and also thanks for inviting me.

00:44:29.560 --> 00:44:33.210
I have one more question
for you I wanted to ask.

00:44:33.210 --> 00:44:36.150
For people wondering
or people debating

00:44:36.150 --> 00:44:41.610
considering incorporating
art into their other non art

00:44:41.610 --> 00:44:44.580
professional lives, or other
things, what advice would

00:44:44.580 --> 00:44:47.340
you have for these
people wanting

00:44:47.340 --> 00:44:50.790
to pursue art in addition to
anything else that you do?

00:44:50.790 --> 00:44:55.450
Given that you have been able
to do it very successfully.

00:44:55.450 --> 00:44:57.580
Thank you for saying that.

00:44:57.580 --> 00:45:04.840
I think what I tell myself
is that if there is something

00:45:04.840 --> 00:45:07.960
that you want to do, do it.

00:45:07.960 --> 00:45:12.880
If you want to take a day
out of your crazy schedule

00:45:12.880 --> 00:45:15.940
and just go out and
take photos, just do it.

00:45:15.940 --> 00:45:20.440
And we all need a
time, need a break,

00:45:20.440 --> 00:45:23.770
we all need a way to express
everything that's building up.

00:45:23.770 --> 00:45:28.660
And I feel like with
our lives now, it's

00:45:28.660 --> 00:45:30.850
everything happening
back to back

00:45:30.850 --> 00:45:32.860
and you don't have a
time to process anything.

00:45:32.860 --> 00:45:36.100
You don't have a time to sit
back and see what is happening.

00:45:36.100 --> 00:45:41.650
And art for most of us
is a way to take out

00:45:41.650 --> 00:45:44.920
all of the things that
have been piling up

00:45:44.920 --> 00:45:49.900
in our bodies and our
mind and just get it out.

00:45:49.900 --> 00:45:54.310
And we need that, you need that
as a way to stay sane and be

00:45:54.310 --> 00:45:58.340
able to operate in
your crazy life.

00:45:58.340 --> 00:46:02.980
So if you have something
that makes you happy, do it.

00:46:02.980 --> 00:46:06.760
Even if you think it's going
to take up from your life

00:46:06.760 --> 00:46:09.070
and keep you from doing
your PSATs, or research,

00:46:09.070 --> 00:46:09.910
or whatever.

00:46:09.910 --> 00:46:13.450
It's not because it's going to
help you take everything that's

00:46:13.450 --> 00:46:17.650
in your mind out and then you
can focus on the other parts

00:46:17.650 --> 00:46:21.130
more too because you
will have a clear mind

00:46:21.130 --> 00:46:25.000
and that will help you the 100%.

00:46:25.000 --> 00:46:26.930
If it didn't, come find me.

00:46:26.930 --> 00:46:31.394
I will be responsible.

00:46:31.394 --> 00:46:33.980
OK, thanks for that.

00:46:33.980 --> 00:46:34.980
Thank you for asking me.

00:46:37.660 --> 00:46:41.050
I will probably add something.

00:46:41.050 --> 00:46:43.750
If you have time,
go model for Elaheh.

00:46:43.750 --> 00:46:46.630
It helps your self-confidence.

00:46:46.630 --> 00:46:50.890
Yeah, it really does.

00:46:50.890 --> 00:46:52.870
I am really
uncomfortable in photos.

00:46:52.870 --> 00:46:58.270
I am really uncomfortable
and just Elaheh

00:46:58.270 --> 00:47:04.100
taking two or three random
or casual pictures of me.

00:47:04.100 --> 00:47:06.630
I felt the confidence boost.

00:47:06.630 --> 00:47:08.170
Yeah.

00:47:08.170 --> 00:47:08.830
She's great.

00:47:08.830 --> 00:47:10.970
You can't separate
her from this project.

00:47:10.970 --> 00:47:13.840
She's a very big
part of this idea.

00:47:13.840 --> 00:47:17.933
It's not easy as--

00:47:17.933 --> 00:47:19.850
at least I don't think
I'm not a photographer,

00:47:19.850 --> 00:47:21.725
but I don't think it's
easy as a photographer

00:47:21.725 --> 00:47:25.090
to make someone comfortable
that you're taking photos of

00:47:25.090 --> 00:47:26.950
and Elaheh is so good at that.

00:47:26.950 --> 00:47:28.180
She's so good at that.

00:47:30.730 --> 00:47:34.660
Thank you for your
amazing music too.

00:47:34.660 --> 00:47:35.500
Thanks.

00:47:35.500 --> 00:47:38.410
For those who didn't know,
the music in the movie

00:47:38.410 --> 00:47:43.030
and in the opening
was composed by Aria.

00:47:43.030 --> 00:47:44.090
And it was amazing.

00:47:44.090 --> 00:47:44.590
Composed.

00:47:44.590 --> 00:47:54.030
Yeah, It was some random
improvises, but thanks.

00:47:54.030 --> 00:47:56.860
[INAUDIBLE] is also here, right?

00:47:56.860 --> 00:47:58.420
Yeah.

00:47:58.420 --> 00:48:01.900
[INAUDIBLE] was the designer
of the exhibition, what

00:48:01.900 --> 00:48:04.900
you're about to
see, and thank you

00:48:04.900 --> 00:48:06.970
so much for making that happen.

00:48:06.970 --> 00:48:10.240
I tried to like change
one or two things

00:48:10.240 --> 00:48:11.600
that I was going crazy.

00:48:11.600 --> 00:48:15.220
So thank you so much
for making that happen.

00:48:15.220 --> 00:48:17.650
Of course, thank you for
all the beautiful art.

00:48:17.650 --> 00:48:19.060
I had such a good
time making it,

00:48:19.060 --> 00:48:22.390
to the point where I'm probably
going to be making more artist

00:48:22.390 --> 00:48:23.050
websites.

00:48:23.050 --> 00:48:24.080
That was amazing.

00:48:24.080 --> 00:48:24.770
Thank you.

00:48:24.770 --> 00:48:26.230
I'm super proud of you.

00:48:26.230 --> 00:48:26.860
Thank you.

00:48:26.860 --> 00:48:28.870
I'm glad you had a good time.

00:48:32.990 --> 00:48:36.100
So we've got some really lively
and inspiring conversation

00:48:36.100 --> 00:48:36.610
happening.

00:48:36.610 --> 00:48:38.860
I want to encourage
that to keep going on,

00:48:38.860 --> 00:48:41.120
but I'm also being
sensitive to the hour.

00:48:41.120 --> 00:48:45.460
So I think we're going to
wrap up the official event

00:48:45.460 --> 00:48:47.690
and we're going to thank
everybody for joining us.

00:48:47.690 --> 00:48:50.410
Thank you so much to
Elaheh for this fantastic

00:48:50.410 --> 00:48:52.420
showing of Trapped.

00:48:52.420 --> 00:48:54.730
On that subject we'd like
to encourage everybody

00:48:54.730 --> 00:48:57.070
in here to visit the
